{"repositoryId":1353188211,"availability":"available","full":"rsasaki0109/3dgs2mesh-web","name":"3dgs2mesh-web","description":"Browser-based 3D Gaussian Splatting to mesh converter powered by Rust, WebAssembly, and Three.js.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":8,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-01T05:53:55Z","updated":"2026-09-01T16:48:33Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://rsasaki0109.github.io/3dgs2mesh-web/","topics":["3d-gaussian-splatting","computer-vision","gaussian-splatting","github-pages","mesh-reconstruction","rust","threejs","webassembly"],"demo":"https://rsasaki0109.github.io/3dgs2mesh-web/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T13:34:14.563Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T13:34:14.563Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T13:34:14.563Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T13:34:14.563Z","stars":8,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Convert PLY, SPZ, SPLAT, KSPLAT, and packaged SOG Gaussian splats into colored, editable triangle meshes—entirely inside your browser.","This is an approximate density-field reconstruction, not an exact implementation of GS2Mesh, SuGaR, GOF, or FGGS-LiDAR. It does not promise research-grade geometric accuracy, manifoldness, or watertight output.","Research pipelines such as GS2Mesh render stereo views and fuse learned depth, while GOF and related methods use training-time information. A static app receiving only one splat asset cannot reproduce those methods faithfully. This project focuses on the useful browser-native subset: anisotropic Gaussian density evaluation, spatial binning, deterministic iso-surface extraction, cleanup, and local export."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/3dgs2mesh-web/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b27ab95dc34892f4a3f2ca324b8eb7b36186df456be8a8dd753e7babc0e158e6","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T13:34:14.677Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T13:34:14.677Z","proje